Description: Read Plasma's configuration folders and Qt 6 font strings
 oxygen-gtk reads kdeglobals and oxygenrc in the folders "kde4-config --path config"
 lists, and finds icon themes in the folders "kde4-config --path icon" lists. Without
 KDE 4 neither command exists, so in a Plasma session the engine merges only its own
 light kdeglobals: GTK 2 programs wear Oxygen's light palette whatever colour scheme,
 font and icon theme the person chose. KDE bug 364693 is the lead: the maintainer,
 Hugo Pereira Da Costa, wrote that the engine "looks for kde4 configuration files in
 the directory list returned by kde4-config --path config" and that "we should
 probably update it to also use the output of kf5-config --path config".
 .
 The technique is openSUSE's qt-config-path.patch (2015, carried by Gentoo since
 2017): the folders Qt lists for QStandardPaths::ConfigLocation, the person's
 XDG_CONFIG_HOME, then XDG_CONFIG_DIRS (where Plasma puts the look and feel's
 kdedefaults before /etc/xdg), come before the engine's own folders. Here the same
 list comes from GLib (g_get_user_config_dir, g_get_system_config_dirs), which every
 GTK 2 program already links, instead of running qtpaths, which Debian ships only as
 qtpaths6; kde4-config is no longer run. The first folder wins, as in KConfig: the
 person's kdeglobals, then kdedefaults, then /etc/xdg, then the engine's own.
 Icon themes are looked for where GTK 2's own icon theme looks: ~/.icons,
 XDG_DATA_HOME/icons, then each XDG_DATA_DIRS/icons.
 .
 Plasma 6 writes fonts as Qt 6's QFont::toString does: 16 fields or more, the weight
 on the OpenType scale (Normal is 400). The engine read that field on Qt 4's scale
 (Normal is 50), so a regular font would be drawn Black once the engine reads
 Plasma's settings. Qt 6's QFont::fromString tells the two forms apart by the number
 of fields; the engine now does the same and brings an OpenType weight to the legacy
 scale with the table of Qt 6's qt_openTypeToLegacyWeight.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos
Origin: vendor, Sparky Stereo OS (queue row 59)
Bug: https://bugs.kde.org/show_bug.cgi?id=364693
Forwarded: no
